etting quite destructive for old lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope the old wiki doesn't split on tribalist lines, it would be a real loss for the fandom.<br /> <br /> The official Paradox wiki seems more focused on giving players and storytellers readily usable informatioms for their game, and it can cohexist just fine with the fan wiki, which is more committed to lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 12-03-2022, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T05:47:31-08:00","id":1498664,"title":"","content":"<i>I support this segregation</i>. Better V5 stays V5 and VTM stays VTM than to encourage any kind of confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T07:16:33-08:00","id":1498673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498664#post1498664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I support this segregation</i>. Better V5 stays V5 and VTM stays VTM than to encourage any kind of confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Even without the poor choice of words, there's again no Edition Warring.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T07:19:48-08:00","id":1498674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498664#post1498664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I support this segregation</i>. Better V5 stays V5 and VTM stays VTM than to encourage any kind of confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking joyfully of segregation, even in game terms, is ... duh.<br /> <br /> Besides from this, it's not a segregation: V5 officialwiki is an official game resource. V5 is the current edition of VTM, and purposefully building walls between segments of the fandom is just something really wrong. It's surely not going to bring back &quot;your&quot; VtM, it's just toxic behaviour arming the franchise and the relations between fans.<br /> <br /> I really hope the old wiki stays a big tent as it is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T07:31:09-08:00","id":1498675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498674#post1498674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Speaking joyfully of segregation, even in game terms, is ... duh.<br /> <br /> Besides from this, it's not a segregation: V5 officialwiki is an official game resource. V5 is the current edition of VTM, and purposefully building walls between segments of the fandom is just something really wrong. It's surely not going to bring back &quot;your&quot; VtM, it's just toxic behaviour arming the franchise and the relations between fans.<br /> <br /> I really hope the old wiki stays a big tent as it is now.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Please don't comment on other posters that have already been criticized by the mods. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T07:51:30-08:00","id":1498676,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer, just my opinion. Perhaps it qualifies as edition warring, I find these things difficult to judge myself, so I'll let moderation decide:<br /> <br /> Even if it's just putting V5 information in its own section on the wiki, separate from the information for other editions, I feel like some form of official gap between 1e - 20th and the new games needs to be put in by this point. Like the Ravnos and Sabbat are wholesale different between 20th to 5th. (Not a WoD specific issue of mine. It's a feeling I actually got looking at the Forgotten Realms wiki sometimes. It's been a while since I've been there, but edition updates sometimes left lore and mechanics all over the place and pre-3.5e stuff just didn't seem to be there sometimes. (This page is still using 3.5, that one's 4th! Wait, is this one 5th?) V20 also had slightly different lore to previous editions (The Rossellini as a revenant family, a great chunk of DAV20, etc), and I would support having that in its own edition specific section too.)<br /> <br /> Let's leave aside one's personal opinions on whether V5 is a legitimate update or a reboot. Even if it is a fifth edition of Vampire: the Masquerade it's part of a universe that <i>isn't </i>the 5th edition of <i>the World of Darkness</i>. It could be the perfect continuation ever but it's part of a whole with gamelines that, despite the name, are not continuations of Hunter: the Reckoning and Werewolf: the Apocalypse. What, VtM fans can have more of their setting, but fuck everyone else? Overwriting VtM's wiki lore is (supposedly) legitimate in such a case (and yet still very irritating if you want the older lore), because it's a continuation, but H&quot;5&quot; and W&quot;5&quot; are going to need their own pages (or else you're just wholesale pushing out a game people still love and play to be replaced by another different one, which is... not going to go well.) This is a fucking mess that only looks to get messier, and I feel some kind of boundaries need to be put somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T06:19:29-08:00","id":1498757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498676#post1498676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disclaimer, just my opinion. Perhaps it qualifies as edition warring, I find these things difficult to judge myself, so I'll let moderation decide:<br /> <br /> Even if it's just putting V5 information in its own section on the wiki, separate from the information for other editions, I feel like some form of official gap between 1e - 20th and the new games needs to be put in by this point. Like the Ravnos and Sabbat are wholesale different between 20th to 5th. (Not a WoD specific issue of mine. It's a feeling I actually got looking at the Forgotten Realms wiki sometimes. It's been a while since I've been there, but edition updates sometimes left lore and mechanics all over the place and pre-3.5e stuff just didn't seem to be there sometimes. (This page is still using 3.5, that one's 4th! Wait, is this one 5th?) V20 also had slightly different lore to previous editions (The Rossellini as a revenant family, a great chunk of DAV20, etc), and I would support having that in its own edition specific section too.)<br /> <br /> Let's leave aside one's personal opinions on whether V5 is a legitimate update or a reboot. Even if it is a fifth edition of Vampire: the Masquerade it's part of a universe that <i>isn't </i>the 5th edition of <i>the World of Darkness</i>. It could be the perfect continuation ever but it's part of a whole with gamelines that, despite the name, are not continuations of Hunter: the Reckoning and Werewolf: the Apocalypse. What, VtM fans can have more of their setting, but fuck everyone else? Overwriting VtM's wiki lore is (supposedly) legitimate in such a case (and yet still very irritating if you want the older lore), because it's a continuation, but H&quot;5&quot; and W&quot;5&quot; are going to need their own pages (or else you're just wholesale pushing out a game people still love and play to be replaced by another different one, which is... not going to go well.) This is a fucking mess that only looks to get messier, and I feel some kind of boundaries need to be put somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, whether it is or not full of retcons, it isn't considered such or a reboot by Paradox.<br /> <br /> It's continued the official continuation of the line and lore.<br /> <br /> It's not really a matter of opinion, it's the update and official and that's final.<br /> <br /> It's also weird to compare it to V20 because, as much as its popular, V20 <u>REMOVED ALL THE METAPLOT </u>until Beckett's Jyhad Diary.<br /> <br /> You can't comment on how big of a retcon the Ravnos have gotten in V5 without commenting on V20 not having the Clan destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T06:27:22-08:00","id":1498758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498662#post1498662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope the old wiki doesn't split on tribalist lines, it would be a real loss for the fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of that is going to be decided by how different community actors engage with it, and with what intent. I've seen other places people be quite open about wanting to purge the unofficial wiki of all 5th edition material. Which really won't help with the already-existing 'edit wars' that have been going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T07:40:02-08:00","id":1498760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498758#post1498758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of that is going to be decided by how different community actors engage with it, and with what intent. I've seen other places people be quite open about wanting to purge the unofficial wiki of all 5th edition material. Which really won't help with the already-existing 'edit wars' that have been going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case, I guess we did need a properly moderated official wiki.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T08:08:26-08:00","id":1498762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498757#post1498757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, whether it is or not full of retcons, it isn't considered such or a reboot by Paradox.<br /> <br /> It's continued the official continuation of the line and lore.<br /> <br /> It's not really a matter of opinion, it's the update and official and that's final.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't intend to deny V5 is a continuation, just acknowledging that others do and putting that aside. <i>My own</i> problem arises when I start getting a literal headache because the rest of the WoD so far, by official declaration, <i>isn't</i>.<br /> <br /> Editions change things and tweak things. They can be placed (and are placed) in continuity, but looking at them individually all editions 1e through to V5 are like worlds unto themselves if taken in isolation. There's a reason some people favour one edition over the others, be it Revised vs V20 edition wars, sticking to 2e or even the occasional player who doesn't acknowledge that there was anything past the first edition because it stops being the exact same setting with every update. It doesn't disqualify what came after to dislike it. (I mean, over the editions massive changes have been made, such as &quot;There are Chinese ventrue&quot; -&gt; &quot;Lasombra have been playing king maker in Imperial China since forever&quot; -&gt; &quot;Chinese vampires are descended from an undead chaos god, the Japanese clans adapt to their environment and are descended from the <i>kami</i> Hiruko&quot; -&gt; &quot;Kindred of the East is its own splat and the VtM regulars have never had a foothold there, ever&quot; -&gt; &quot;We have never heard of this &quot;<i>wan gui</i>&quot; you speak of.&quot;)<br /> <br /> While V5 is a <i>massive</i> overhaul, I won't reject it as a form of VtM just because of that, however jarring these changes might be. But WoD gamelines usually come together. WtA was WtA from 1 e - 20th, VtM VtM from 1e - 20th. Whatever changes they underwent, big or small, however disconnected the gamelines are from each other, they usually &quot;went together&quot; as part of a whole WoD edition. (Hunter, admittedly only had a gameline in Revised, but I still think using its name for something else was rude and KotE, in the same boat, no longer exists at this point. Not a problem for me, but still unfortunate for the fans and has a knock-on effect on the wider WoD.) WoD5 is a jumble of continuation and reboot and as a whole now confuses the shit out of me and is bound to lead to arguing and confusion.<br /> <br /> Having some form of organisation won't stop people screaming at each other, but at least will make it easier to navigate and find specifically what you're looking for, and help keep editions stepping on each others toes. Nor does V5 need singling out for this treatment, since all editions vary, though it will likely need more space due to a bigger amount of mechanical changes (as such its own wiki is a good idea) and any crossover content is going to bring problems because W5 is not the setting that would've crossed over with V20 and previous. Maybe it doesn't matter in the long run, but it is a paradox that make my head hurt to think about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also weird to compare it to V20 because, as much as its popular, V20 <u>REMOVED ALL THE METAPLOT </u>until Beckett's Jyhad Diary.<br /> <br /> You can't comment on how big of a retcon the Ravnos have gotten in V5 without commenting on V20 not having the Clan destroyed. </div> </div> </div>V20 left it up to players if the Week of Nightmares was canon in their games or not, same with the various curses placed on the Children of Haqim. I didn't consider &quot;massive metaplot events may or may not have occurred according to your preferences&quot; on the same level as &quot;this clan now has a totally different weakness, a completely different discipline spread, and their signature discipline is now a different thing (Chimestry used to affect tech and had vague Changeling connections, now it's just Obfuscate).&quot; YMMV.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T09:39:44-08:00","id":1498771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498757#post1498757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't comment on how big of a retcon the Ravnos have gotten in V5 without commenting on V20 not having the Clan destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we got Ravnos Revised. That was a story about a Clan that was deeply damaged, not destroyed. So they changed and adapted, and even became better than before. A lot of what V20 does is inspired by what Revised did, even if it tries to rollback some of the metaplot to make it more &quot;timeless&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498760#post1498760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's the case, I guess we did need a properly moderated official wiki.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do. The problem was oddly coming from the New side of the divide just cutting old material and replacing it with new. And honestly neither of these extremes are what we need. We need a well curated wiki that can separate two streams and tell us where we can refer to any of the data. I want to be able to refer to any White Wold book without wondering what someone cut or who wants to have a edit war or prefers V1 to V5. I just want info from all the sources and I'll be the judge of what is of value to me. I think many of us are like this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 12-04-2022, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T16:59:28-08:00","id":1498808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498760#post1498760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's the case, I guess we did need a properly moderated official wiki.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be entirely fair, a lot of it (from second-hand knowledge, so YMMV I guess) seemed to be very overzealous individuals (often new users) removing information and replacing it with new. Which I can see depending on what fandoms and wikis the individuals are already involved in and how those pieces of fiction are concerned. Hanlon's Razor really applies in this instance, from what others who are more involved have said elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498771#post1498771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do. The problem was oddly coming from the New side of the divide just cutting old material and replacing it with new. And honestly neither of these extremes are what we need. We need a well curated wiki that can separate two streams and tell us where we can refer to any of the data. I want to be able to refer to any White Wold book without wondering what someone cut or who wants to have a edit war or prefers V1 to V5. I just want info from all the sources and I'll be the judge of what is of value to me. I think many of us are like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the other thing to consider with the official wiki is that one of the big goals is to remove the barrier of all that metaplot that bogs down games for new players. Which is why the official wiki isn't touching on any of the old material except in the broadest of strokes at times. A well-curated wiki with both is great, don't get me wrong, but I don't think it's fully what WoD is worried about, insofar as old material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 12-04-2022, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T23:38:16-08:00","id":1498823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498771#post1498771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But we got Ravnos Revised. That was a story about a Clan that was deeply damaged, not destroyed. So they changed and adapted, and even became better than before. A lot of what V20 does is inspired by what Revised did, even if it tries to rollback some of the metaplot to make it more &amp;quot;timeless&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> We do. The problem was oddly coming from the New side of the divide just cutting old material and replacing it with new. And honestly neither of these extremes are what we need. We need a well curated wiki that can separate two streams and tell us where we can refer to any of the data. I want to be able to refer to any White Wold book without wondering what someone cut or who wants to have a edit war or prefers V1 to V5. I just want info from all the sources and I'll be the judge of what is of value to me. I think many of us are like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It makes more sense to just separate contradictory material from previous editions, rather than replacing one edition's info with another.<br /> <br /> So you can have &quot;V5 Lore&quot;, followed by &quot;Classic Lore&quot;, with subdivisions of the latter if needed (e.g., &quot;Revised Lore&quot;, &quot;V20 Lore&quot;).<br /> <br /> Part of the appeal of the WoD is that the lore has always been loose enough to let you do a lot with it. Hence the constant use of unreliable narrator and the frequent embracing of contradictory lore.<br /> <br /> If someone editing the wiki comes from a fandom where canon is more concrete, they may not have got that, and so may have made good-faith edits without that key piece of context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T07:37:23-08:00","id":1498853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki#post1498649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a part of the Paradox wikis, this seems to be their source of truth on all things V5. <a href=\"https://vtm.paradoxwikis.com/VTM_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">https://vtm.paradoxwikis.com/VTM_Wiki</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this, it is nice to see another VtM wikipedia-style site that is done to a good enough level. Hopefully it will be supported and developed further. Certainly the Clan pages could be more extensive, and definitely more illustrations would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T09:06:51-08:00","id":1498866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498853#post1498853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for this, it is nice to see another VtM wikipedia-style site that is done to a good enough level. Hopefully it will be supported and developed further. Certainly the Clan pages could be more extensive, and definitely more illustrations would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you want or mean by extensive. They've explicitly said the official wiki is V5-based and V5-sourced, so things in pre-V5 editions won't be added until they're mentioned in V5. So you won't see Dignitas and such on the Ventrue page, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T08:45:37-08:00","id":1499281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498649-v5-gets-an-official-wiki?p=1498866#post1498866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on what you want or mean by extensive. They've explicitly said the official wiki is V5-based and V5-sourced, so things in pre-V5 editions won't be added until they're mentioned in V5. So you won't see Dignitas and such on the Ventrue page, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just like more descriptions, of varied and novel categories, which would summarize or analyze VtM's lore, facts, legends, meta, motifs, and themes. Discussion of particular interpretations, subjective view points or changes throughout the books would also be an interesting addition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}